  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Encyclical Workshop for staff and partners.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">An encyclical is a letter issued by the Pope to the churches worldwide, i.e. to bishops, priests, religious people, and the whole faithful Catholic world.  Usually, the Pope also includes in the addressees all people of good will.  
 The themes which Francis is likely to address are ones around human dignity, authentic and integral human development, and human ecology. In Church teaching, human ecology means that both the human person and nature are to be respected, and that human beings must care for and protect the natural environment, adopting an attitude of wonder and contemplation before it, and rejecting a culture of waste and indifference.</narrative>
  </description>
